# =============================================================================
# Immix: recycled blocks and idle mutators, and exhaustion among garbage
# =============================================================================
# A long-lived list built among short-lived garbage leaves partly free blocks
# after every collection. Those must reach the thread that allocates rather
# than idle threads (scala-native#5168), and once the heap is at its cap and
# effectively full the allocator must throw OutOfMemoryError instead of
# collecting again for every few allocations (scala-native#5169). That limit
# follows the JVM's: low yield and collection-dominated time over several
# collections in a row, so a heap that is full but still making progress runs.

> runIdleMutators
> runFragmentedExhaustion
> set nativeConfig ~= (_.withMode(scala.scalanative.build.Mode.releaseFast))
> runIdleMutators
> runFragmentedExhaustion
